# The `agent-router` group, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped — the
# manifest is their one home) — the rules file that agent-router.promtool-test loads. Not a
# manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules
# (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded
# directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY
# *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would fail it.
#
# This is the SECOND fixture pair over openrouter-proxy/prometheusrule.yaml. The first,
# subscription.promtool-{rules,test} (#288), covers the OTHER group — `claude-subscription` — and
# its own re-copy recipe hard-selects `select(.name == "claude-subscription")`, so running THAT
# header's command after editing an `agent-router` alert copies nothing you changed and the
# fixture passes vacuously. One file per group is what keeps the two recipes honest; do not merge
# them.
#
# ⚠ NOT DRIFT-PINNED (like both existing hand copies here and unlike github-exporter's
# queued-age.promtool-rules, which `devbox run exporter-self-test` checks): the general harness
# that would extract `.spec.groups` at run time and delete the hand copies altogether lives in
# `scripts/**` + `.github/**`, CI-invoked paths outside the fixer lane's tier. Until it exists,
# RE-COPY AFTER EVERY EXPR EDIT — a stale copy tests the OLD expr and passes vacuously:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups":[{"name":"agent-router","rules":[.spec.groups[] | select(.name == "agent-router") | .rules[]]}]}' argocd/resources/openrouter-proxy/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#
# …then re-attach this header. The command is deliberately ONE LINE: yq 4.x's lexer rejects a
# newline inside the expression ("lexer: invalid input text"), so the pretty-wrapped form used in
# github-exporter/loop-health.promtool-rules' header does not actually run as written. Verified
# byte-identical against the body below on 2026-08-11 (homelab#332).
#
# The regression witnesses live in a SEPARATE pair, agent-router-witness.promtool-{rules,test},
# rather than in a second group here the way #288/#313 did it. That is forced, not stylistic:
# promtool evaluates every rule in every loaded rule file at every step of every test, and the
# pre-#332 OpenRouterKeyBudgetLow expr ERRORS (many-to-one on `on (key)`) whenever two series
# share a `key` — which is precisely the input of this file's §masking case. Keeping the witnesses
# out lets the shipped-behaviour fixture model a scaled-out proxy at all. See that file's header.
groups:
  - name: agent-router
    rules:
      - alert: RouterDbEphemeral
        expr: router_db_persistent == 0
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: Router store is running ephemeral (:memory:)
          description: 'The openrouter-proxy router store failed to open its PVC and degraded to :memory: — strikes, provider events, generation costs and the persisted 429 latch are lost on every restart. Check the openrouter-proxy-data PVC / Longhorn volume in ns agent-egress.'
      - alert: RouterRotationStale
        expr: max by (source) (max_over_time(router_rotation_age_seconds{source="openrouter-daily-rankings"}[10m])) > 259200
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: OpenRouter rankings rotation feed is stale (>3d)
          description: The dailyish list-daily-model-rankings pull has not written rotation entries for {{ $value | humanizeDuration }} — check proxy logs for MCP/Cloudflare failures (the UA gotcha) and the router-account-key Secret.
      - alert: OpenRouterKeyBudgetLow
        expr: max by (key) (max_over_time(router_openrouter_key_limit_remaining_usd[10m])) / on (key) max by (key) (max_over_time(router_openrouter_key_limit_usd[10m])) < 0.10
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: OpenRouter key {{ $labels.key }} below 10% of its spend limit
          description: Standing key {{ $labels.key }} has {{ with query (printf "max by (key) (max_over_time(router_openrouter_key_limit_remaining_usd{key='%s'}[10m]))" $labels.key) }}{{ . | first | value | humanize }}{{ end }} USD left under its limit — OpenRouter-rail dispatch for that project will die on 402s when it empties.
      - alert: OpenRouterCapacityDown
        expr: router_openrouter_capacity_down == 1
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: OpenRouter account is capacity-down
          description: 'OpenRouter account-scope capacity has been latched for 30m — worker dispatch is degrading to the haiku subscription rail or deferring the OpenRouter rail. Probe: GET openrouter-proxy.agent-egress:8080/router-status → .openrouter_capacity (reason / remaining_s / recent_429_models) names which leg latched. The credit leg reads the openrouter-operator''s openrouter_account_credit_usd gauge (openrouter-operator-metrics.openrouter-operator:9090), NOT OpenRouter directly — .credit_poll_failures climbing there, or router_openrouter_credit_poll_failures_total here, means that leg is blind and only the data-plane legs (hard-402 / cross-model 429s) can still fire (homelab#180).'
      - alert: RouterRunModelDrift
        expr: max by (rail, stack, role, requested, served) (max_over_time(router_run_model_drift_total[10m])) > 0
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: OpenRouter/Go rides served a model different from the one requested ({{ $labels.stack }}/{{ $labels.role }})
          description: '{{ $value }} OpenRouter/Go ride(s) on {{ $labels.stack }} requested {{ $labels.requested }} but the /generation harvest (or Go ledger) shows they were SERVED as {{ $labels.served }} — a silent model redirect, the PR#407 class (a claude/haiku dispatch ran the CLI default opus for 23 days). Chainless alias remapping (slot maps, failover ladders) multiplies the places this can happen. The claude-harness/subscription rail has its own belt (agent_model_drift on github-exporter); rides whose served side is ABSENT are RouterRunModelUnverifiable, not this alert.'
      - alert: RouterRunModelUnverifiable
        expr: max by (rail, stack, role, requested) (max_over_time(router_run_model_unverifiable_total[10m])) > 0
        for: 30m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: OpenRouter/Go rides have NO served-side evidence ({{ $labels.stack }}/{{ $labels.role }})
          description: '{{ $value }} OpenRouter/Go ride(s) on {{ $labels.stack }} requested {{ $labels.requested }} with NO served-side record in the router store for 30m — a /generation harvest miss, a Go ledger gap, or a ride that never produced telemetry. Absence never reads as agreement (the FU-108/FU-125 silent-success class): the belt is blind to what served them. Check openrouter_generation_harvest_total{outcome="missed"} (a rising ratio = the harvest is half-blind) before assuming the rides were healthy.'
